    {
      "id": "8b1dbf43-1117-4da1-99cf-f4301ef4b12a",
      "category": "All",
      "order": 1,
      "faqs": [
        {
          "id": "a5ed6ab1-a791-4f28-a2be-68e8e59444ea",
          "question": "Am I eligible for the CMA program?",
          "answer": "To be eligible for the US CMA program, you\u2019ll need to meet these criteria:\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Education: You\u2019ll need a bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution. But, if you\u2019re still pursuing your degree, you can take the CMA exam now and meet the education requirement within 7 years of passing the exam.\r\n2.Membership: You must become a member of the Institute of Management Accountants (IMA).\r\nThe minimal eligibility criterion lets you start your CMA journey while finishing your education.",
          "order": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "f947f8ed-8913-42b0-8ca6-569850083eaa",
          "question": "What is the CMA course structure?",
          "answer": "The US CMA course is structured to provide in-depth knowledge in financial management and business strategy. It consists of two comprehensive parts:\r\nPart 1: Financial Planning, Performance, and Analytics\r\nThis section focuses on:\r\n1.External Financial Reporting Decisions\r\n2.Planning, Budgeting, and Forecasting\r\n3.Performance Management\r\n4.Cost Management\r\n5.Internal Controls\r\n6.Technology and Analytics\r\nPart 2: Strategic Financial Management\r\nThis part covers:\r\n1.Financial Statement Analysis\r\n2.Corporate Finance\r\n3.Decision Analysis\r\n4.Risk Management\r\n5.Investment Decisions\r\n6.Professional Ethics\r\nEach part is a four-hour exam consisting of multiple-choice questions and essay-based scenarios, designed to assess your analytical skills and decision-making capabilities.\r\nWith Miles' support, you can complete both parts within 12 months.\"",
          "order": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "ee7298c1-d0a5-4763-a639-9fc7f5a9262c",
          "question": "What are the requirements for the CMA license?",
          "answer": "To earn your US CMA (Certified Management Accountant) license, here\u2019s what you\u2019ll need:\r\n1.Education: A bachelor's degree from an accredited institution, or you can qualify with a professional certification like CPA, CA, or an equivalent.\r\n2.Exam Completion: Pass both parts of the CMA exam, which covers financial planning, analysis, control, and decision-making.\r\n3.Work Experience: Two years of professional experience in management accounting or financial management. This can be done before or within seven years after passing the exam.\r\n4.IMA Membership: You\u2019ll need to be a member of the Institute of Management Accountants (IMA), the body that grants the CMA certification.\r\n5.Ethics: Adhere to the IMA\u2019s Statement of Ethical Professional Practice.\r\nOnce you've met these requirements, you'll earn the prestigious CMA certification, giving you top recognition in management accounting.\"",
          "order": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "8d8e7909-d493-4f9e-89eb-609171f4e39a",
          "question": "What is the fees structure for the CMA program?",
          "answer": "Here\u2019s a breakdown of the estimated total costs for the CMA exam:\r\nMiles CMA fees\r\nIMA Membership Fee (students: 3 years; professionals: 1 year) + GST 18%\r\nExam fee (payable to IMA)\r\nTotal: Around INR 1.06 lakhs\r\nAt Miles Education, we\u2019re transparent about the costs, and we\u2019ll support you every step of the way to help you achieve your CMA dreams!\r\nFor more details, check out \r\n\r\nhttps://www.mileseducation.com/accounting/us-cma/schedule-and-fees.",
          "order": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "0680a8fa-a86b-417b-9f40-bc0721798095",
          "question": "When are the CMA exams conducted?",
          "answer": "The US CMA exams are offered during three testing windows each year, giving you the flexibility to choose a time that works best for you:\r\n1.January \u2013 February\r\n2.May \u2013 June\r\n3.September \u2013 October\r\nThis gives you the flexibility to choose a location that\u2019s convenient for you. Once you receive your Notice to Schedule (NTS) from the IMA, you can book your exam at a nearby Prometric centre.",
          "order": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "2dda97b1-925d-4d09-a284-a21743588106",
          "question": "Where is the Miles CMA Program available?",
          "answer": "Miles Education offers a blended learning experience. You can attend live training sessions at our Miles Stadium of Learning in 9 cities across India, or access online video lectures from anywhere.\r\nAs a Miles CMA candidate, you\u2019ll also get 220+ hours of one-on-one mentoring, live online training with our experts, and over 100 classroom and webinar sessions to support your journey.",
          "order": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "7ab8e5a6-4ec8-4314-81d3-7903112a6bd2",
          "question": "Why should I pursue the CMA program?",
          "answer": "With just 2 exams in 12 months, the US CMA program sets you up for fantastic job opportunities in India. You\u2019ll have access to roles at 220+ MNCs and Fortune 500 companies right here, making it a great way to fast-track your career.",
          "order": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "82941f66-217f-474a-90b6-ce16b6e35352",
          "question": "Why should I consider US CMA over Indian CMA?",
          "answer": "Choosing the US CMA can offer you a broader range of opportunities. Here\u2019s why:\r\nGlobal Credential: While the Indian CMA focuses on the local market, the US CMA is widely recognized by multinational corporations in India, making you more competitive for roles in these companies.\r\nVersatility: The US CMA covers areas like financial planning, analysis, and decision-making, making you highly valued across various industries. This gives you the flexibility to explore roles in finance management, business analysis, and strategy.\r\nHigher Earning Potential: US CMA professionals tend to earn higher salaries within India, as their skills are sought after by top employers.\r\nCareer Growth: With the US CMA, you\u2019ll be well-positioned for leadership roles in MNCs and top firms in India, helping you advance faster in your career.\r\nIf you\u2019re looking for a career with Big 4 and MNCs in India, the US CMA is a smart choice.",
          "order": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "2b296827-ec4e-4e95-8012-9fe2eb226ea2",
          "question": "How do I get started with the CMA program?",
          "answer": "Getting started with the US CMA program is simple:\r\n1.Join IMA: First, sign up as a member of the Institute of Management Accountants (IMA), which administers the CMA program.\r\n2.Register for the CMA Program: Once you're an IMA member, you can enroll in the CMA program and register for the exams.\r\n3.Meet the Educational Requirements: You'll need a bachelor's degree, but if you're still studying, you can take the exam and fulfill the education requirement within 7 years of passing.\r\n4.Prepare for the Exams: Start preparing with a solid study plan. Miles Education offers live and online training to help guide you through the two-part CMA exam.\r\n5.Schedule Your Exams: Pick a testing window at a Prometric center near you and register for the exam.\r\n6.Complete the Experience Requirement: You'll need two years of professional experience in accounting or finance, which can be done either before or within 7 years of passing the exam.",
          "order": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "74e9a9f6-7c2c-4e73-b6dc-56b25b2b5222",
          "question": "Why should I consider CPA over CA?",
          "answer": "If you're thinking global, CPA is your ticket to international opportunities. While CA is highly respected in India, CPA gives you recognition that crosses borders, especially in the US With the US in need of accountants, the demand for CPAs is at an all-time high, making it a great pathway to land jobs at top US accounting firms.\r\nIf your career vision goes beyond India, CPA is definitely worth considering.",
          "order": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "3672df67-4b37-405c-9498-5296f3307319",
          "question": "What are the requirements for the CPA license?",
          "answer": "Once you\u2019ve cleared all 4 CPA exams, you can apply for your CPA license from any of the 55 state boards. While each state has its own rules, most require you to have 150 credits and at least 2 years of work experience. You'll also need to complete the \u201c3+1 Es\u201d:\r\n1. Examination - Pass the CPA exam.\r\n2. Education - If you need extra credits, Miles can help with a bridge course.\r\n3. Experience - Licensed CPAs at Miles can verify your work experience.\r\n4. Ethics - Complete an online ethics course.\r\nNo need to stress\u2014Miles Education will guide you through the entire process, start to finish.",
          "order": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "0ae3248a-a1b4-46bf-a982-49d01a8c4489",
          "question": "What is the fee structure for the CPA program?",
          "answer": "Here\u2019s a breakdown of the estimated total costs for the CPA exam:\r\nMiles CPA fees Evaluation fee (paid to the evaluation agency) Exam fee (paid to the US state board) Total: Around INR 3.85 lakhs\r\nWith Miles Education, we ensure transparency in the process, and we\u2019ll be with you every step of the way to help you achieve your CPA dreams!\r\nFor more details, you can check out this link.",
          "order": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "94f87cc1-404f-4e7f-a766-30191ecd54f3",
          "question": "When should I start and complete the program?",
          "answer": "You can start your CPA journey right after finishing your Bachelor's degree in India. Once you're ready, just enrol and connect with our Game Plan team\u2014we'll create a personalized roadmap to help you complete your CPA in the next 16 months.\r\nWhether you're targeting certain recruitment cycles or career milestones, we\u2019ll make sure your plan fits your schedule, balancing work and study.",
          "order": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "1e5cfe86-0a64-4b0e-a967-adf23feb89ee",
          "question": "When are the CPA exams conducted?",
          "answer": "The CPA exams are offered year-round, so you can schedule each section when it works best for you. The exam is available during four testing windows:\r\nJanuary \u2013 March\r\nApril \u2013 June\r\nJuly \u2013 September\r\nOctober \u2013 December\r\nThis flexible schedule lets you plan your exams around your study pace, giving you the freedom to tackle the four sections at your own convenience.",
          "order": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "bce78523-326d-421a-b7b8-9968aea663b9",
          "question": "Where can I take the CPA exam?",
          "answer": "In India, you can take the CPA exam at Prometric testing centers in cities like:\r\nBangalore\r\nHyderabad\r\nMumbai\r\nNew Delhi\r\nAhmedabad\r\nChennai\r\nKolkata\r\nYou\u2019ll have the flexibility to pick a location that\u2019s convenient for you. Once you get your Notice to Schedule (NTS) from the State Board, you can book your exam at a nearby Prometric center.",
          "order": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "9fb2c793-9172-4f5c-b3fd-1dde22ffaf3b",
          "question": "Where is the Miles CPA Program available?",
          "answer": "Miles Education offers a blended learning experience. You can attend live training sessions at our Miles Stadium of Learning in 9 cities across India, or access online video lectures from anywhere.\r\nAs a Miles CPA candidate, you\u2019ll also get 220+ hours of one-on-one mentoring, live online training by our experts, and over 100 classroom and webinar sessions to support your journey.",
          "order": 7
        },
        {
          "id": "0eb55731-b1f2-4a71-8a08-ab38fcdf2f03",
          "question": "Who is eligible for the CPA program?",
          "answer": "US qualifications are designed to complement your university education. To appear for the US CPA exam, you\u2019ll need at least 120 credits (or 90 credits under a pre-education option). For the CPA license, you\u2019ll need 150 credits.\r\nAs a general rule, every year of university education in India equals 30 semester credits in the US So, it breaks down like this:\r\nB.Com: 3 years x 30 credits = 90 credits\r\nB.Com + M.Com/MBA: 90 credits + 60 credits = 150 credits\r\nB.Com + CA/CS/CWA: 90 credits + 60 credits = 150 credits\r\nCA/CS/CWA: Recognized by some states as 2-3 years of US education\r\nThis makes the CPA program quite accessible for many professionals in India!",
          "order": 8
        },
        {
          "id": "206393fe-923f-4ced-93da-dd8bb25b26eb",
          "question": "Who conducts the CPA exam?",
          "answer": "The CPA exam is conducted by the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA), the top authority in the accounting world. They partner with the National Association of State Boards of Accountancy (NASBA) to make sure the exam meets the highest standards and aligns with state licensing requirements in the US\r\nPassing this prestigious exam opens up global opportunities and sets you up for top-tier accounting roles!",
          "order": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "0aba10a3-339f-421a-8163-b3accbcb461a",
          "question": "Who awards the CPA license?",
          "answer": "The CPA license is awarded by individual State Boards of Accountancy in the US Each state has its own board that grants the license once you\u2019ve passed the CPA exam, met the education and experience requirements, and adhered to ethical standards.\r\nThis CPA license will open a world of career opportunities in accounting!",
          "order": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "c6b64b49-38a5-481c-8f47-c5223e745329",
          "question": "How do I get started with the CPA program?",
          "answer": "Getting started with the CPA program is easy:\r\n1. Check your eligibility: Make sure you\u2019ve completed your Bachelor\u2019s degree and meet the educational requirements for the CPA exams.\r\n2. Register with Miles Education: Visit your nearest Miles office or connect with our experts online. We\u2019ll guide you through everything\u2014from exam registration to setting up your personalized study plan.\r\n3. Craft your Game Plan: Our Game Plan team will create a tailored 16-month roadmap that fits your goals, balancing your study and work efficiently.\r\n4. Access your resources: As a Miles CPA candidate, you\u2019ll get instant access to Varun Jain\u2019s recorded videos, online test banks, one-on-one mentoring, live online classes, and weekend options. We've got everything covered!\r\nWith the right preparation and support, you'll be well on your way to becoming a CPA!",
          "order": 11
        },
        {
          "id": "38eef77c-6b79-4b76-9679-e543c4a21763",
          "question": "WHAT is the fee structure for the Miles US Pathway program?",
          "answer": "The total cost of the Miles US Pathway program is approximately $48,000. However, you only need around $2,000 upfront, with the rest covered by student loans. Here\u2019s how Miles helps reduce your costs:\r\n1. Credit Transfer: Thanks to our collaboration with JAGSoM, an AACSB-accredited B-School in India, you complete 30% of your coursework in India. This reduces your US university tuition by up to 50%, and in some cases, even 70%.\r\n2. Scholarships: Miles partners with US universities to secure scholarships, leveraging both the high quality of our talent pool and our cohort size (20+ students per university). This approach makes the program far more affordable while still offering a top-tier education and extended work opportunities in the US.",
          "order": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "798219cb-b0b6-439e-99be-b7bbb870016a",
          "question": "WHAT are the universities that are available?",
          "answer": "Miles partners with over 30+ universities, including top-ranked institutions like Michigan State University and Rutgers University. We also offer location-specific options, such as Pace University and Fordham University in New York, DePaul University in Chicago, and Seattle University in Seattle. While Miles supports job placements, your university choice isn\u2019t critical to your job prospects. For more guidance, reach out to our US Pathway team\u2014they\u2019ll help you choose the best university for your needs.",
          "order": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "708454c2-bb19-4b16-ad08-3ea2f734300c",
          "question": "WHAT is the refund policy?",
          "answer": "Although we boast over a 90%+ visa acceptance rate, if your US visa faces rejection (twice), we assure you a full refund of your 20K fee.",
          "order": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "feec0ece-a41a-45e5-8a71-e13d0eadcfac",
          "question": "WHEN are the admissions open?",
          "answer": "Admissions for the Miles US Pathway program are open year-round, allowing you to apply at any time. However, US university intakes typically happen during the Fall (August/September) and Spring (January) semesters. It\u2019s best to start your application process early to ensure you meet the deadlines for your preferred intake. The Miles team will guide you through the admissions process and help you choose the best intake based on your timeline and preferences.",
          "order": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "201dfad7-831d-4244-a66c-9ff4d985c7f6",
          "question": "WHEN should I start and complete the program?",
          "answer": "Ideally, you should start the Miles US Pathway program at least 8-10 months before your preferred intake. Currently, admissions are open for Fall 2025.",
          "order": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "8b95e6a8-19c4-4893-af23-c7aff619b951",
          "question": "WHO is eligible for the Miles US Pathway program?",
          "answer": "To be eligible for the Miles US Pathway program, you generally need to have completed 4 years of university education, equivalent to the US undergraduate requirement. If you have a B.Com/BBA along with an M.Com/MBA or professional qualifications like CA/CS/CWA, you're already eligible. If you have only a B.Com/BBA from a NAAC A university with a first division, you are eligible. If you still do not meet the above criteria, don\u2019t worry! Miles offers a university bridge course for just INR 30K. The best part? It\u2019s fully integrated with the CPA coursework, so there are no additional studies beyond your CPA preparation.",
          "order": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "d5f362bf-80e8-494f-8c7a-1cc2e9fd8dd4",
          "question": "How can I cancel my event booking?",
          "answer": "To cancel your event booking, follow these steps:\r\nStep 1: Go to the hamburger menu on top left of your app and select Bookings.\r\nStep 2: Select Manage Booking for the event you want to cancel.\r\nStep 4: Tap on Cancel Appointment.",
          "order": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "bede6b42-ab25-480b-b69d-6f22b9b3f87a",
          "question": "How can I change my event booking slot?",
          "answer": "To cancel your event registration, you follow these steps:\r\nStep 1: Go to the hamburger menu on top left of your app and select Bookings.\r\nStep 2: Select Manage Booking for the event you want to cancel.\r\nStep 4: Change your booking details based on your needs.\r\nStep 5: Save your changes.",
          "order": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "b9158736-9820-4dfe-82a7-6a9183eb605d",
          "question": "How can I book a spot for a tailored event?",
          "answer": "To book a spot for a tailored event, follow these steps:\r\nStep 1: Go to the navigation bar on the bottom of your app and select Events.\r\nStep 2: Choose the Tailored Event you want to attend. \r\nStep 3: Update the details required to book the event.\r\nStep 4: Tap on Book Now.",
          "order": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "3b9a325d-aae2-4c57-8baa-59621e3e4d20",
          "question": "Where can I find the joining link for the session?",
          "answer": "You can find the joining link on the event booking page. Along with this, you will even receive an Email & Whatsapp message with the event link and prerequisites.",
          "order": 4
        },
        {
          "id": "f424d640-746c-4345-8bdc-b837005e4398",
          "question": "Where can I find the address of the nearest Miles office?",
          "answer": "Once you book a Miles Office visit, you can find the nearest Miles Office address along with a google maps link on the top of the event page. Along with this, you will even receive Email & Whatsapp communication with the required information and other prerequisites.",
          "order": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "e8316d1d-7727-431d-9718-ad70db2b8889",
          "question": "Can I enroll into the Miles CPA program if I am not a graduate?",
          "answer": "To be eligible for the Miles CPA program, you need to have graduation in Commerce and Accounting or a professional qualification like CA (Chartered Accountant), CMA (Cost and Management Accountant), Intermediate passed, or CS (Company Secretary).",
          "order": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "612f8b62-c4f4-474b-a4aa-2d7bec5f63ad",
          "question": "I am unable to make my enrollment payment.",
          "answer": "Please reach out to your student relations point of contact to resolve this query.",
          "order": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "1d9cc3ce-1bfb-491b-8159-b21cc58ea792",
          "question": "I want a deadline extension for fee payment.",
          "answer": "Please reach out to your student relations point of contact to resolve this query.",
          "order": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "1503ca7c-6ac0-4628-99cc-0a37063ae7b0",
          "question": "How can I cancel my enrollment for a program?",
          "answer": "Please reach out to your student relations point of contact to resolve this query.",
          "order": 4
        },
        {
