      "glossary": "<div style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: #0d1a2d; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; padding: 20px; margin: 10px auto; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); max-width: 800px; line-height: 1.6;\">\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  <div style=\"margin: 15px 0; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;\"><h3 style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.2;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Episode 1: AI in the Audit Workflow&nbsp;</strong></h3><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Agentive.</strong> A company focused on building AI tools designed specifically for audit workflows. Its goal is to reduce repetitive manual work and improve efficiency through purpose-built software.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Assertions.</strong> Statements or claims that management makes in financial records and reports, which auditors evaluate during testing. Common examples include accuracy, cutoff, and classification.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Audit workflow.</strong> The sequence of steps, tasks, and procedures followed during an audit engagement. It includes activities like requesting documents, testing transactions, reviewing support, and documenting conclusions.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Burnout.</strong> A state of physical or mental exhaustion caused by prolonged stress, overload, or repetitive work demands. In professional settings, it often reduces motivation, focus, and long-term job satisfaction.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Citation-based.</strong> A method of review or analysis that ties findings back to specific source material or supporting evidence. This approach improves traceability and helps make conclusions easier to verify.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Classification.</strong> The process of assigning financial transactions to the correct categories in accounting records and reports. Proper classification helps ensure information is organized accurately and presented clearly.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Cutoff.</strong> An accounting concept used to determine whether transactions are recorded in the correct reporting period. It helps ensure income and expenses are recognized at the right time.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Expense testing.</strong> An audit procedure used to examine recorded expenses and verify that they are valid, accurate, and properly supported. It helps identify errors, misstatements, or compliance issues in expense-related transactions.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Financial statement review.</strong> A structured examination of financial statements to identify inconsistencies, risks, or potential issues. It often involves checking disclosures, presentation, and alignment with supporting records.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Grant revenue testing.</strong> An audit procedure used to verify that grant-related income is recorded correctly and supported by appropriate documentation. It helps confirm that revenue recognition follows the relevant terms and requirements.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Product design.</strong> The process of planning and developing products that solve user problems effectively and efficiently. It combines functionality, usability, and user needs to shape how a tool works in practice.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Repeatable.</strong> Describes a consistently performed process across different tasks or engagements. Repeatable methods improve reliability, efficiency, and standardization.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"></p><h3 style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.2;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Episode 2 : AI Agents, Not Chatbots, for Audit</strong></h3><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"></p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Agentic workflows.</strong> Structured AI-driven processes that carry out a sequence of connected tasks rather than answering a single prompt. They are designed to follow steps, use evidence, and move through a workflow in a more operational way.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Billable time.</strong> The hours a professional records and charges to a client for work performed. It is often used to measure effort, cost, and engagement profitability.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Client friction.</strong> Difficulty, delay, or frustration experienced by clients during a process or interaction. It often appears when requests are unclear, repetitive, or harder to complete.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Client portal.</strong> A secure digital space where clients can upload files, view requests, and exchange information with a service provider. It helps centralize communication and document sharing.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Core audit platform.</strong> The primary software system used by a firm to manage audit work, documentation, and engagement processes. It acts as the main operational base for carrying out audit procedures.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Evidence gathering.</strong> The process of collecting documents, records, and supporting information needed to evaluate whether a procedure or conclusion is supported. It is a key part of validating results and identifying exceptions.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Exceptions.</strong> Items or results that do not match expectations, criteria, or supporting records during a review or test. They are flagged for further examination because they may indicate an error, inconsistency, or risk.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">General ledger.</strong> The central record that contains a company\u2019s financial transactions organized by account. It serves as a foundation for preparing reports and verifying financial activity.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Materiality.</strong> A threshold used to judge whether an item, error, or omission is significant enough to influence understanding or decisions. It helps determine what deserves closer attention in financial review.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Multi-step tool use.</strong> The ability of software or AI to complete a task through several connected actions rather than a single response. This can include extracting data, comparing values, checking conditions, and returning results.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Professional judgment.</strong> The informed decision-making that relies on expertise, experience, and careful evaluation of facts and circumstances. It is essential when interpreting results, assessing risks, and reaching conclusions.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Request list.</strong> A structured list of documents or information that a client is asked to provide for a review or engagement. A clear request list improves efficiency by making expectations easier to understand and fulfill.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"></p><h3 style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.2;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Episode 3: Grant Revenue Testing in Agentive</strong><br></h3><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Bulk upload.</strong> A feature that allows multiple files or documents to be uploaded at the same time instead of one by one. It helps speed up document collection and makes large-scale processing more efficient.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Conditional evidence.</strong> Supporting documentation used to determine whether specific requirements or conditions have been met. It helps verify timing, fulfillment, and related criteria tied to a transaction or agreement.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Contributions.</strong> Resources such as cash or other assets given to an organization without an equal exchange in return. They are often provided to support a purpose, program, or initiative.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Deep analysis.</strong> A more intensive review process that examines information in greater detail to generate richer findings or conclusions. <br><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Donor-imposed restrictions.</strong> Limitations placed by a donor on how funds or assets may be used by the recipient. These restrictions help define the purpose, timing, or conditions attached to a contribution.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Grant agreement.</strong> A formal document that outlines the terms, amount, purpose, and conditions of a grant. It serves as a key source for understanding what was awarded and how it should be supported.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">OCR.</strong> Short for optical character recognition, a technology that converts text in scanned files or images into readable digital text. It makes document contents searchable and easier for software to analyze.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Prompt injection.</strong> A technique used to insert referenced values or instructions into a prompt so the system can evaluate a specific item dynamically. It allows the same logic to adapt based on changing inputs or records.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Sampling.</strong> A method of selecting a portion of items from a larger group for review or testing. It is used to examine representative items without evaluating every single entry.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Selections.</strong> Chosen transactions, records, or items pulled from a larger data set for testing or review. They act as the specific entries against which supporting documents and procedures are applied.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Tick mark legend.</strong> A reference guide that explains the meaning of symbols or marks used in a work paper or review file. It helps users interpret whether items passed, failed, or require further attention.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Work paper.</strong> A document or file used to record procedures performed, evidence reviewed, and conclusions reached during a professional engagement.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"></p><h3 style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.2;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Episode 4 : Expense Testing in Agentive</strong></h3><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"></p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Bank statements.</strong> Financial records provided by a bank that show deposits, withdrawals, and other account activity over a period of time. They help confirm whether recorded transactions were actually processed through the account.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Calendar year.</strong> A twelve-month period that runs from January 1 through December 31. It is often used as a standard time frame for organizing records, reporting activity, and checking whether entries fall in the correct period.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Counter evidence.</strong> Information that suggests a result may not match as expected or that raises doubt about a conclusion. It is useful in review because it highlights areas that may require closer attention or follow-up.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Fiscal year.</strong> A twelve-month accounting period used for tracking financial activity and reporting results. It may match the calendar year or follow a different start and end date depending on the organization.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Invoice.</strong> A document issued by a seller that lists goods or services provided and the amount owed. It serves as supporting evidence for charges, dates, vendors, and payment details.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Journal entry.</strong> A formal record used to enter financial transactions into an accounting system. It typically includes accounts affected, amounts, dates, and descriptions that help track how a transaction was recorded.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Match results.</strong> The output showing whether related records or documents have been linked successfully based on selected criteria. These results help users see if supporting files appear to correspond to the transaction being reviewed.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Operating expense.</strong> A cost incurred through the normal day-to-day running of an organization or business. Examples can include travel, software, meals, training, or hosting expenses tied to routine operations.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Reasoning.</strong> The explanation behind how a result, conclusion, or recommendation was reached. In a review process, reasoning helps users understand the logic used and its soundness.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Receipt check number.</strong> A numeric reference associated with a payment or transaction record that helps identify and connect it to supporting documentation. It can be used to trace activity across receipts, statements, and internal records.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Software expenses.</strong> Costs related to software products or services used by an organization, such as subscriptions, platforms, or digital tools.<br><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Vendor name.</strong> The name of the supplier or business that provided a product or service. It is an important identifying detail used to match documents and confirm who a transaction relates to.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"></p><h3 style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.2;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Episode 5: Financial Statement Review in Agentive<br></strong></h3><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Batch email updates.</strong> Automated email summaries sent at set intervals to keep team members informed about comments, changes, or review activity. They help people stay aligned without needing to check the system constantly.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Column header.</strong> A label at the top of a column that identifies the type of data shown beneath it. It helps organize information and makes comparisons across values easier and more consistent.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Comparative statements.</strong> Financial statements that present figures from more than one period side by side for comparison. They help readers identify changes, trends, and inconsistencies across reporting periods.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Cross-footing.</strong> A process of checking whether totals remain accurate when values are added across rows and columns in a financial table. It helps confirm that different parts of a statement mathematically agree with one another.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Internal consistency.</strong> The degree to which the same information matches throughout a single document. It helps ensure that repeated figures, labels, and references do not conflict with each other.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Mathematical accuracy.</strong> The correctness of calculations, totals, and numeric relationships within a document or data set. It is essential for ensuring that reported values are reliable and free from arithmetic error.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Members equity.</strong> The residual interest in an organization\u2019s assets after liabilities are considered, often shown in statements for certain entity types. It reflects the accumulated value attributable to the members of the organization.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Prior year consistency.</strong> A check to confirm that values carried forward or presented comparatively from an earlier year still match the previously reported figures. It supports continuity and reduces the chance of mismatched historical numbers.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Review checklist.</strong> A structured list of items used to guide and document a review process. It helps ensure important checks are completed in a consistent and organized way.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Rounding error.</strong> A small difference in a number caused by rounding values up or down during calculation or presentation. While often minor, it can still create visible inconsistencies in reports and statements.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Row heading.</strong> A label placed beside a row to identify the category or line item associated with the values in that row. It provides context for interpreting the numbers across a table or statement.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><br></p><h3 style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.2;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Episode 6: Why AI-Native Audit Tools Win<br></strong></h3><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Architectural reality.</strong> The practical limitations and constraints created by the way a software system is originally designed. It reflects how deeply the structure of a platform affects what can be added, changed, or improved later.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Backwards compatibility.</strong> The ability of newer software or systems to continue working with older data, features, or processes. It is often important for large platforms that need to avoid disrupting existing users and workflows.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Busy season.</strong> A period of especially high workload when teams face tighter deadlines, heavier volumes, and greater pressure. It often tests the efficiency of systems, staffing, and day-to-day processes.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Client experience.</strong> The overall impression and quality of interaction a client has while working with a company, service, or team. It is shaped by responsiveness, clarity, efficiency, and ease of collaboration.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Coverage.</strong> The extent to which a process, review, or system examines the full range of relevant items, risks, or activities. Greater coverage can improve confidence that important areas have been addressed.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Data models.</strong> Structured ways of organizing information so software can store, connect, and use it effectively. They shape how data moves through a system and how easily new capabilities can be built on top of it.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Distribution.</strong> The process or mechanism through which a product, platform, or service reaches its users or customers. In business strategy, strong distribution can be a major advantage because it affects adoption and market reach.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Incumbents.</strong> Established companies or providers that already hold a strong position in a market or industry. They often have scale, existing customers, and mature products, but may move more slowly than newer entrants.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Ingested.</strong> Processed and brought into a system so the information can be read, organized, and used. In digital workflows, documents or data are ingested before they can be analyzed or connected to other tasks.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Retention crisis.</strong> A situation in which an organization or industry struggles to keep people over time. It usually signals deeper problems related to workload, tools, satisfaction, or long-term career sustainability.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Startup.</strong> A newly built company created to solve a specific problem, often with a focus on speed, experimentation, and innovation. Startups typically operate with concentrated resources and a narrower mission than large established firms.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><strong style=\"color: #ffffff;;\">Switching costs.</strong> The time, effort, expense, or disruption involved in moving from one product, platform, or provider to another. High switching costs can make organizations hesitate even when better options become available.</p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><br><br></p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><br><br><br></p><p style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px 0; line-height: 1.6;;\"><br></p></div>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size: 14px; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center; color: #ffffff; opacity: 0.8; width: 100%;\">\r\n<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0; text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;\">\r\n  <hr style=\"flex: 1; border: 0; height: 1px; background: #ffffff; width: calc(100% - 150px);\" />\r\n  <img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/masterclass-bucket-usa2/media/web-app/miles-masterclass.logo.webp\" alt=\"Miles Masterclass Logo\" style=\"width: 150px; height: auto; margin: 0;\" />\r\n</div></div>\r\n</div>",
