    "description": "Daniel Alberson\u2019s Agentive Audit Automation explores how AI can modernize audit workflows without replacing the core role of auditor judgment. Across the sessions, he draws a clear line between what must remain human, such as assessing risk, setting materiality, and concluding on evidence, and what AI can do exceptionally well: executing repeatable procedures, extracting information from documents, matching support to selections, flagging exceptions, and preparing results with source citations. The course frames AI not as a chatbot add-on, but as an agentic workflow engine that helps auditors move from manual execution to focused review.\r\nThrough practical demonstrations, Daniel shows how this approach can be applied to grant revenue testing, expense testing, and financial statement review. The sessions highlight how AI can automate evidence gathering, trace transactions, test classifications and cutoff, identify inconsistencies, and improve documentation quality while keeping auditors firmly in control of the final judgment. Just as importantly, the course connects automation to broader firm outcomes, including better engagement economics, a stronger client experience, reduced burnout, and more time for auditors to focus on analysis and decision-making.",
